---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const notes = [
  {
    date: 'Nov 2026',
    tag: 'agents',
    title: 'An agent that finishes is not an agent that is right',
    body: [
      'The first version of my agent harness measured success as "the run completed". That number looked great and meant almost nothing. A run can complete with a half-finished refactor, a test suite it edited to pass, or a change a reviewer would reject in ten seconds.',
      'What actually predicts trust is narrower: did the change survive review, and would the next person understand why. That is harder to instrument, which is exactly why most agent benchmarks skip it.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: 'Oct 2026',
    tag: 'retrieval',
    title: 'Chunking is a product decision wearing an engineering costume',
    body: [
      'Chunk size looks like a tuning parameter. It is not. It decides what a retriever can ever return, so it silently sets the ceiling on answer quality before a model is involved.',
      'The useful move was to evaluate chunking against the questions people actually ask, not against a generic relevance set. Retrieval quality stopped being a number and became a list of specific questions we could not answer.',
    ],
  },
  {
    date: 'Sep 2026',
    tag: 'permissions',
    title: 'Authorization should be re-checked per tool call, not per session',
    body: [
      'A session that was authorized an hour ago is a historical fact, not a permission. When tools act on real systems, the check has to happen at the moment of the call, against the caller as they are now.',
      'Building the OAuth + PKCE flow this way cost more than a session-scoped token, and it removed an entire class of "the agent did something the user could not have done" bug.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Field notes"
  description="Short notes on agent reliability, retrieval and permissions — written from work rather than reading."
>
  <section class="wrap" style="padding-block: var(--s8) var(--s6)">
    <p class="eyebrow">Field notes</p>
    <h1 class="display" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); margin-top: var(--s3)">
      Short things I learned the hard way.
    </h1>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-top: var(--s4)">
      Not essays. One observation each, usually from a mistake, always from something built.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" style="padding-bottom: var(--s9); max-width: 78ch">
    {notes.map((n) => (
      <article class="note">
        <p class="note__meta">{n.date}<br />{n.tag}</p>
        <div>
          <h3>{n.title}</h3>
          {n.body.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
        </div>
      </article>
    ))}

    <p class="meta" style="margin-top: var(--s6); text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0">
      Longer write-ups are in progress. If you want one on something specific — agent
      evaluation, RAG failure modes, MCP permissions — <a class="link-plain" href="mailto:sanjumsanthosh@gmail.com">ask</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
